privacy-contents = Contents
privacy-picture-title = Profile picture
privacy-picture = A profile picture is optional. If you choose one, your browser makes a square copy of it without the photo's details (such as place, camera or time) and sends that. Where your browser does not allow this, it sends the file itself, and Central's converter keeps only its pixels. Central turns it into a 256 × 256 pixel AVIF and PNG picture that holds nothing else, and if the picture moves, also into an animation (AVIF, at most 100 frames) made from its frames alone by a converter program (ffmpeg) that never sees your file. It stores them with a fingerprint (a SHA-256 digest of the PNG and of the animation, if there is one) and the time you set it, under a random key that changes with every new picture. The converter runs as a separate process for each picture and keeps nothing. Everyone can see your picture, people who are not signed in included, at its address, and it is shown beside your display name. It is kept until you replace or remove it, an administrator removes it, or you delete your account, and is then deleted at once. A browser that showed it may keep a copy for up to an hour. Anyone signed in can report a picture with a reason and an optional note: the report holds the reporting account, the picture's fingerprint, the reason, the note and the time. Administrators see who reported it, and the person whose picture it is never does. If an administrator removes your picture, you are told when and why, and new pictures may be blocked for a time. Decided reports are kept for one year. Per account, Central counts uploads (ten an hour, thirty a day). Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR for the picture, and Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR for reports, the counts and moderation (our legitimate interest in keeping the service free of unlawful and abusive content).
privacy-challenges-title = Daily and Weekly challenges
privacy-challenges = Central keeps attempts, results, hints used, ranking preferences and permanent badge progress with your account. The official host sends the game's result and measured time. Names, tags and scores are public only when you enable the ranking for that task, and disabling it removes them from the ranking. These records remain until account deletion, with the backup periods described under Account. Challenge metadata is included in your account's data export.
tower-title = The Verdant Tower
tower-privacy = Central stores your expedition runs, chosen improvements, remaining lives, results, ranking preferences and permanent relic progress with your account. Only your public name, tag and best eligible score appear when you enable a season's ranking. Disabling it removes that listing. Your account export includes expedition runs and attempts. Account deletion also deletes this progression, subject to the backup periods described under Account.
privacy-ranked-title = Ranked play
privacy-ranked = For ranked play Central keeps with your account: your entries in the queue (format, season, your Elo rating and a fingerprint of your deck), the games it pairs you for (opponent, gateways, your approval of them and their terms, times, result), your decks as fingerprints of the cards with their counts, never a deck name or notes, and per format, season and deck your Elo rating, games, wins, losses and draws, placement progress, league, division, badges and the sleeves and playmats they unlock. While a game runs, Central also holds its opening, both decks and both players' decisions and decision time, so that a second gateway can check it or take it over after an outage; Central deletes these after the game ends, usually within minutes, at the latest the following day. A game's gateways receive, only after you approved them and their current terms, an identifier for that game instead of your account ID, together with your deck and the game; they can be in any country. Your connection to the game runs through Central, so the gateway does not see your IP address. Your opponent sees your display name and tag. The boards of every season are public, signed in or not: whoever played a rated ranked game in a season is listed there with display name, tag, Elo rating, league, division, games, wins, losses and draws, even with their player profile turned off; the deck board also shows an identifier of the deck from which its cards cannot be read. A program computes Elo rating, league and the choice of opponents from your results; this has no legal or similarly significant effect on you. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (the ranked games you want to play). Central deletes queue entries daily once they are a day old; everything else is kept until you delete your account, and for backups the periods under "Your account" apply. These data are part of your account's data export.
privacy-donate-title = Donations
privacy-donate = The donation page links to GitHub Sponsors (GitHub, Inc., USA), Liberapay (Liberapay, France) and Ko-fi (Ko-fi Labs Limited, United Kingdom). Only when you follow one of these links does your browser connect to that platform. Payment happens there and with its payment service (Stripe or PayPal), and the platform's own privacy notice applies. We take no payment on this site. The page shows how much of the monthly goal is covered and what was given once. Baylee Central collects these figures, not your browser: it asks Liberapay for its public total and GitHub Sponsors for the account's own totals and one-time sponsorships, without the sponsors' names, takes the euro exchange rates from the European Central Bank, and is notified by Ko-fi of each payment. Of a payment Central keeps only the amount, the currency, the time, whether it was given once or regularly, and a fingerprint of the platform's transaction number so that a notice that comes twice counts once. Everything else in a notice, such as a name, an e-mail address or a message, is discarded without being stored or logged. After 40 days the amounts are added to a total and the single records are deleted. The figures name nobody, and we publish no donor's name.
